From 1ccef77a651da027094fbafb8b0d0cf02e69443e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <services.claude@accounts.ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 21:58:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0288 -- fix unsigned wrap in the TAS stall-frame delta

0286 computed the per-frame accumulator delta as an unguarded unsigned
subtraction, now_ns - last_ns. last_ns can legitimately be AHEAD of now_ns:
now_ns is sampled once at the top of run_tick_fixed, while the freeze/thaw
guards (0280 load_stage, 0285 on_song_start) set last_ns to "now" from inside
the catch-up loop, after that sample. The subtraction then wrapped to a delta
of tens of days, sailed past the 150 ms stall test, and clamped an ordinary
gameplay frame to a single tick.

Measured on g2k, v1.6.7 PG 1: 485 of 503 "stall frames" in the AdLib cell and
478 of 488 in the GUS 20-voice cell were this wrap, every one reporting
4154504685 ms. The OPL3 and WaveBlaster cells, which stall far less often,
showed 12-16 discounts of 168-442 ms -- all genuine -- and replayed the full
route. The corrupted cells did not: G22 and G23B truncated and GC5 skipped
Assembly Hall entirely.

The LOG_INFO cast to (unsigned) truncated the value to 32 bits, which is why
it read as a merely large number instead of an obvious wrap. Widened to
unsigned long long so a future wrap is unmistakable.

Fix: treat a backwards delta as zero elapsed. The interval it would describe
was already excluded by whichever guard moved last_ns forward, so zero is the
correct contribution, not a clamp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index a66dfcd7..d3001d39 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -889,7 +889,20 @@ static void run_tick_fixed(void)
     // Normal play is untouched: outside TAS the delta is unclamped and the
     // catch-up behaviour is bit-for-bit the pre-0281 path.
     // Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TAS_FT_GUARD=0 (shared with 0280).
-    Uint64 delta_ns = now_ns - last_ns;
+    // patch 0288: last_ns can legitimately be AHEAD of this frame's now_ns.
+    // now_ns is sampled once at the top of run_tick_fixed, but the freeze/thaw
+    // guards (0280 load_stage, 0285 on_song_start) set last_ns = "now" from
+    // INSIDE the catch-up loop, i.e. after that sample. The unsigned
+    // subtraction below then wrapped, producing a delta of tens of days, which
+    // sailed past the 150 ms stall test and clamped an ordinary frame to one
+    // tick. Measured on g2k: 485 of 503 "stalls" in the AdLib cell were this,
+    // all reporting 4154504685 ms -- and the LOG_INFO cast to (unsigned)
+    // truncated the value to 32 bits, disguising it as merely a large number
+    // rather than an obvious wrap.
+    //
+    // Treat a backwards delta as zero elapsed: the interval it would describe
+    // was already excluded by whichever guard moved last_ns forward.
+    Uint64 delta_ns = (now_ns >= last_ns) ? (now_ns - last_ns) : 0;
 
     // DOS-PORT (patch 0286): during TAS replay, a frame that overran by more
     // than any plausible gameplay budget is a STALL (a load), not slow
@@ -920,7 +933,7 @@ static void run_tick_fixed(void)
     if (TAS::replaying() && tas_stall_discount_active() && delta_ns > STALL_NS)
     {
       LOG_INFO("tas: stall frame {} ms -> contributing 1 tick (patch 0286)",
-                (unsigned)(delta_ns / 1000000));
+                (unsigned long long)(delta_ns / 1000000));
       delta_ns = TICK_NS;
     }
     else if (TAS::replaying() && tas_ft_clamp_active() && delta_ns > TICK_NS)
